  "working_tree": "Uncommitted code-intelligence work; this receipt and documentation follow the frozen checks.",
  "shared_implementation": "The shared resource interpreter retains created-object provenance through moves, child changes, rollback and cleanup. Both native workers use one descriptor-bound receipt implementation and the existing bounded native Revision/Observation reader. Thin journal adapters do not choose separate recovery policies.",
  "contract": [
    "New native creation receipts persist descriptor identity and an opaque native stat/attribute revision before creating a file anchor. The revision predicts exactly one anchor link; matching and last-link cleanup account only for that application-owned link transition. Existing revision-less receipts retain their earlier identity/empty-content contract rather than sampling a new baseline.",
    "Attribute comparison includes the existing bounded xattr/ACL/semantic-flag digest. Mode, ownership and ordinary file link count, size and modification time remain checked through publication and rollback. Creation publication itself permits ctime changes; tracked directory namespace changes do not exempt attributes or ownership.",
    "Native staging may touch a created parent even when the child is never published. A bounded immutable namespace intent is persisted before that syscall, bound to the exact transaction, plan, parent receipt ordinal and native identity. Recovery validates complete and partial intent metadata, preserves unknown metadata and cleans intents before removing their original receipt. The root-parent fast path avoids a receipt scan.",
    "Actual original-service/HMAC acceptance and SQLite worker admission previously deleted an externally updated empty created file after lost acknowledgement in both native modes. Updated Local and Remote tests expire the original service/grant, invalidate provider settings, then preserve file/directory permission, modification-time, xattr, ACL and nodump changes and added file hard links. Unchanged controls roll back normally. No action query, command dispatch or editor successor is replayed.",
    "Native fault contracts preserve changed attributes at every recorded creation boundary, including unpublished objects and the final empty file anchor. Controls cover every creation/rollback primitive and database acknowledgement. Archived receipt recovery and complete, partial and invalid namespace intent cases remain covered.",
    "Fresh installed Local and Remote resource, command, interrupted recovery and declared-input workflows pass with the immutable original LanguageReview and fresh authority only for initial dispatch. The native ownership contracts pass on macOS and Linux; browser fixtures do not replace native permission-prompt evidence."
  ],
